.TH L_GSSIAM_AUTH 8 2026-03-24 Lustre "Lustre Configuration Utilities"
.SH NAME
l_gssiam_auth \- Handle Lustre GSSIAM security flavor server authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY l_gssiam_auth
.RB [ -v
.IR VALIDITY_DURATION ]
.I KEY
.I TOKEN_ENCODED
.I SUBDIR
.I UPCALL_NAME
.I OPTIONS
.YS
.SH CONFIGURATION
The behavior of the auth upcall and downcall mechanism is configured via
sysfs/lctl tunables on the server.
.SS Server Tunables
.TP
.B sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_auth_upcall
Specifies the path to the executable invoked by the MDS to validate GSSIAM
tokens. The default is
.B /usr/sbin/l_gssiam_auth
and can be changed using:
.RS
.B lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_auth_upcall=/path/to/auth_upcall
.RE
.TP
.B sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_auth_downcall
A write-only sysfs file used by the auth upcall to return validation results
(permissions, Project ID, expiration) back to the MDS.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B l_gssiam_auth
is the server-side counterpart invoked by the MDS. When the MDS receives an
GSSIAM
.B SEC_CTX_INIT
RPC from a client containing a token and subdirectory, it calls the binary
defined in gssiam_auth_upcall, which defaults to l_gssiam_auth,
to validate the token against the enterprise GSSIAM service. If the token is
valid and authorized for the requested subdirectory,
.B l_gssiam_auth
returns the mapped user permissions (Read-Only, Read-Write, etc.) and the
associated Project ID via the
.B gssiam_auth_downcall
interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -v \fIVALIDITY_DURATION\fR
(Optional) Specifies the validity duration of the token in seconds.
Defaults to 600.
.TP
.B \fIKEY\fR
The hash key pre-computed by the kernel for this authentication request.
This key must be returned in the downcall to identify the cache entry.
.TP
.B \fITOKEN_ENCODED\fR
The base64url encoded GSSIAM token provided by the client.
.TP
.B \fISUBDIR\fR
The specific subdirectory (fileset) the client is attempting to access.
.TP
.B \fIUPCALL_NAME\fR
The name of the upcall cache (e.g., gssiam_server) used to construct the
sptlrpc/<upcall_name>/gssiam_auth_downcall path.
.TP
.B \fIOPTIONS\fR
The options bitmask provided by the client's mount command (e.g., client read-only flag).
This is a bitwise OR of one or more of the following mount option flags:
.RS
.TP
.B 0x01 (GSSIAM_OPT_RDONLY)
The client mounted the filesystem as read-only (e.g., via
.BR "\-o ro" ).
.TP
.B 0x02 (GSSIAM_OPT_DISABLE_ROOT_SQUASH)
The client mounted the filesystem with root squashing disabled (e.g., via
.BR "\-o disable_rootsquash" ).
.RE
.SH DOWNCALL FORMAT
The helper must write the authentication result back to the target's
.B gssiam_auth_downcall
lprocfs/sysfs file using the following format:
.RS
.EX
.B <key> <mount_option>:<expire>:<approved_options>:<principal>
.EE
.RE
.PP
Where:
.TP
.B \fIkey\fR
The opaque request key passed as the first argument to the upcall.
.TP
.B \fImount_option\fR
The security permission granted by the authentication service:
.B rw
for read-write access,
.B ro
for read-only access,
.B deny
to deny access, or
.B expired
for an expired token.
.TP
.B \fIexpire\fR
The duration (in seconds) that this authentication token remains valid.
.TP
.B \fIapproved_options\fR
A decimal integer bitmask of approved mount options. Currently,
.BR 2 " (" GSSIAM_OPT_DISABLE_ROOT_SQUASH ")"
is supported to allow disabling root squash. The kernel ignores this bit
unless the client also requested it with
.BR "\-o disable_rootsquash" .
.TP
.B \fIprincipal\fR
The authenticated principal string of the client. This field is mandatory
when \fImount_option\fR is \fBrw\fR or \fBro\fR, and is optional (may be empty)
when \fImount_option\fR is \fBdeny\fR or \fBexpired\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure the server authentication upcall path:
.RS
.EX
.B lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_auth_upcall=/sbin/my_gssiam_auth
.EE
.RE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B l_gssiam_auth
command is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.17.57.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_57
